{"timestamp":"2026-09-01T10:35:57.016Z","ordinal":16975,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a05669-fc4c-7aa0-b9a1-034d833ed8ed","turn_id":"01a05c89-fe2e-77c2-88ef-bf8b5d9c5248","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6911705c-bf5a-4f24-8686-45e136547f0d","process_id":"7545","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","docker exec tiered-serve bash -lc '\ncd /root/projects/vllm\nsed -n \"5220,5380p\" vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py\nprintf \"RECENT PLANNER LOGS\\n\"\ngrep -RhsE \"Tiered-serve KV:|Tiered-serve budget:|dedicated request shrank|hugepage alloc: total=\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/logs/serving/llama_3_1_70b_instruct/cao-cd3-fused/*/server.log 2>/dev/null | tail -24\n'"],"cwd":"file:///home/ubuntu","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"docker exec tiered-serve bash -lc '\ncd /root/projects/vllm\nsed -n \"5220,5380p\" vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py\nprintf \"RECENT PLANNER LOGS\\n\"\ngrep -RhsE \"Tiered-serve KV:|Tiered-serve budget:|dedicated request shrank|hugepage alloc: total=\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/logs/serving/llama_3_1_70b_instruct/cao-cd3-fused/*/server.log 2>/dev/null | tail -24\n'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\n                # D + O = N; ensure O ≤ o_max and D ≤ d_max_hbm\n                # Dedicated blocks must be >= 16 (matches core.py).\n                # When D is forced up to MIN_DED, O is reduced so\n                # the HBM constraint (D*L*pb + O*pb ≤ gpu_avail)\n                # still holds.\n                MIN_DED = 16\n                # Explicit dedicated request via env (BLOCKS direct, or SIZE_GB\n                # -> blocks).  When set, HONOR it (capped to what HBM holds) and\n                # cap offloadable at the LPDDR buffer (o_max); the usable total\n                # then shrinks below num_blocks_total and the leftover blocks\n                # stay UNALLOCATED (empty HBM/LPDDR is fine).  Without it, keep\n                # the default (force dedicated up so offloadable == o_max and\n                # the full block budget is used).\n                _env_ded = None\n                if os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_BLOCKS\"):\n                    _env_ded = int(\n                        os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_BLOCKS\"))\n                elif os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_SIZE_GB\"):\n                    _gb = float(\n                        os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_SIZE_GB\"))\n                    if _gb > 0 and per_block_bytes_raw > 0 and n_kv_layers > 0:\n                        _env_ded = int(_gb * 1024**3\n                                       // (n_kv_layers * per_block_bytes_raw))\n                if _env_ded is not None:\n                    num_dedicated_hbm = max(\n                        MIN_DED,\n                        min(_env_ded, d_max_hbm, num_blocks_total - 1))\n                    num_offloadable_lpddr = min(\n                        num_blocks_total - num_dedicated_hbm, o_max)\n                else:\n                    num_dedicated_hbm = max(\n                        MIN_DED,\n                        min(d_max_hbm,\n                            num_blocks_total - o_max,\n                            num_blocks_total - 1))\n                    # Determinism: vLLM's profiling measures gpu_avail with a few\n                    # MB of run-to-run jitter -> num_dedicated_hbm flips by +-1\n                    # block run-to-run, which SHIFTS the dedicated/offloadable\n                    # boundary (block_id >= num_dedicated => offloadable).  With\n                    # the KV-offload pipeline that changes WHICH blocks are\n                    # offloaded+recompressed and makes the decode nondeterministic\n                    # (a boundary request's tokens diverge run-to-run).  Round the\n                    # boundary DOWN to a stable granularity so the jitter is\n                    # absorbed; the few reclaimed blocks just become offloadable.\n       